  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would introduce a new takeaway to the District&nbsp;Centre, which would sit in close proximity to schools within 400m and walking distance of the site; those of which include Ripple Primary School and Eastbury Primary School. This is in direct conflict with London Plan Policy E9.&nbsp; The proposal would be detrimental to health objectives and fails to demonstrate that other benefits would outweigh this. As such, the proposal is found to be in conflict with the following policies, which when taken together seek to ensure that development is appropriately located, contributes positively to District Centres and promotes health and wellbeing:National Planning Policy Framework (December, 2024)Policies SD6, SD8 and E9 of the London Plan (March, 2021)Policies DME 3 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)Saturation Point: Addressing the Heath Impacts of Hot Food Takeaway SPD (July 2010)"
  ],
